# L §5.19 (round 12): "A fulfils naming an instance that doesn't exist, or one whose legs don't touch the
# observation's places or that has a leg the observation lacks, is refused (RUN-RECORD)"; L §8.4 RUN-RECORD
# "observation <r> fulfils <instance> and lacks its leg <l>". pay has legs fee and main; the bank row (a transfer, one
# leg cash) fulfils it: konto's balance (which books the refused observation) and observed(pay) are refused. (Was
# REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.19, writer 5's T-93: observed() with no observation holding the leg.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind splits: event certain
  leg fee: PLN
  leg main: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input amt: money PLN
input pday: date

move pay: splits
  on pday
  leg fee from konto to world amount amt
  leg main from konto to world amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 5.00 PLN
  pday = 2026-03-02
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-01
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-02, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 10.00 PLN, fulfils: pay) "l1"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask r: observed(pay)
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-RECORD observation bank[r1] fulfils pay and lacks its leg fee
  open: pay
  cut 2026-12-31
r: refused: RUN-RECORD observation bank[r1] fulfils pay and lacks its leg fee
  cut 2026-12-31
